From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] signal: NtGetContextThread reports no hardware
 breakpoints

A request for CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS printed a FIXME and left the
caller's buffer as it came, which an anti-debug check reads as a
debugger's breakpoints. The runtime arms none, so the fields are zero,
as save_context reports them for an exception (0255).

Linear: PLA-514
Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index 275f47d..6bd0d4c 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -7022,7 +7022,17 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtGetContextThread( HANDLE handle, CONTEXT *context )
         context->X[18] = frame->x[18];
         context->ContextFlags |= CONTEXT_ARM64_X18;
     }
-    if (needed_flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) FIXME( "debug registers not supported\n" );
+    if (needed_flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
+    {
+        /* Playport (PLA-514): no hardware breakpoint or watchpoint is set (the
+         * runtime arms none), as save_context reports; the caller's buffer was
+         * left as it came, which an anti-debug check reads as a debugger's. */
+        memset( context->Bcr, 0, sizeof(context->Bcr) );
+        memset( context->Bvr, 0, sizeof(context->Bvr) );
+        memset( context->Wcr, 0, sizeof(context->Wcr) );
+        memset( context->Wvr, 0, sizeof(context->Wvr) );
+        context->ContextFlags |= CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS;
+    }
     set_context_exception_reporting_flags( &context->ContextFlags, CONTEXT_SERVICE_ACTIVE );
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
